My slice generates the dungeon every round, displays it when the user checks the map, and handles the logic for timers and pausing the game.

Dungeon Gen:
dungeonMap.py takes a difficulty and assigns difficulty modifiers based on that, and first generates the minimum number of doors, then rolls to check if every remaining
potential door will become an extra door. Door generation completely restarts if the dungeon is completely interconnected (i.e. you can get to any room from a given point).
Then, it rolls for each room to become an entity based on the modifiers. After that, it displays the newly-generated ASCII dungeon map.

Pausing:
Pausing takes the player who wants to pause, the other player, and the pausing player's inventory and equipment. It asks the other player if they're all right with pausing,
and if so, displays the pause menu to the pausing player. The options are Resume, Inventory, Stats, Options, and Quit.

Timers:
There are three timers: one for the dungeon, one for the round, and one for combat. Each one has two functions, one to initialize the start time and duration from its
arguments, and one to check if the timer has expired.